  "base": "361b2cc",
  "claims": [
    "P2.1. With allow_baseline false and a baseline file, --check --strict exits 1 and names the file, and stats --write-baseline writes nothing; without the setting a project with a baseline exits as before.",
    "P2.2. A local base strictly behind its configured upstream is compared through that upstream with one note: line before the summary; every other state of the base (level, ahead, diverged, no upstream, a commit, a remote-tracking branch, a tag, a name only the remote has) prints what it printed before this diff.",
    "P2.2b. facts --base in the stale state writes on standard output, and to --out, exactly the document that facts --base <upstream> writes, with the note on standard error only; rules_check.py check --base judges against that base.",
    "P2.3. No command of either script starts git fetch, pull, push or remote, in any state.",
    "P2.4. An entry whose reread: line was committed after the last commit to its modules is not listed as older than its code, also when the commits share one second; after a later commit to a module it is listed again; a second reread: line is refused.",
    "P2.5. With count_extra_dirs on, the same-name, no-docstring, over-12-modules groups, the defines-main label and the summary's count cover the extra folders; with it off every line of review is what it was before this diff.",
    "P2.6. dev-tools' own check that no baseline is kept is --check --strict alone, and tests/test_own_index.py holds it through the setting.",
    "The skill, its references, docs/components.html and .devtools/project.md describe what the code now does, and nothing they say is false of it."
  ],
